# SHA-256 of the 17 replay traces of this study. The trace files themselves are not published
# (they are output of the course's generator); this file lets you check a regenerated copy:
#
#     sha256sum -c data/traces.sha256        # from the repository root, traces in traces/
#
# Generator: python -m workloads.generators from the course repository
#   https://github.com/mlleo/inference-engine-study at commit 802a1642fcefc06735a89af054213c9904b4ff45
#   (not included here; bash tools/fetch_course_harness.sh checks it out into .course/).
#   Run the commands below from that checkout's project/ folder, then copy traces/ here.
# Tokenizer: --model Qwen/Qwen3-4B at revision 1cfa9a7208912126459214e8b04321603b3df60c, the snapshot
#   the study used (the server logs name it). With --model the prompt token lengths are exact, so the
#   prompt texts depend on the tokenizer. The generator has no revision flag; to pin the revision,
#   pass a local snapshot folder of that revision as --model.
# The commands are inferred from each file's name and __meta__ line, w3/make_queues.sh and the course
# scripts (scripts/run_baseline.sh for reasoning.jsonl, scripts/cross_replay.sh for the *_x files).
# Re-checked on 2026-10-02 against the generator functions: arrival_time, max_new_tokens and rid
# match for all 17 files. The prompt texts were not regenerated (that needs the tokenizer).
# Every trace sets ignore_eos=True, so each request generates exactly max_new_tokens tokens.
#
# Used by: reasoning (qps 0.35) = 09-06, 09-07 and 09-13 runs; q0.5 q0.6 q0.8 q1 q2 q4 q8 = 09-07 sweep
# (q0.5 q1 q2 q4 again on 09-13); q0.2 = 09-13 deterministic runs; q2_s0.3 q2_s1.0 q2_m1000 = 09-13;
# *_x = 09-13 cross replay.

